<title>CANADA: CBRS says reaffirms Saskatchewan debt ratings.</title>
<headline>CBRS says reaffirms Saskatchewan debt ratings.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Bond Rating Service said on Thursday that it had reaffirmed an A rating for Saskatchewan's long-term debt and an A-1 rating on the province's short-term debt.</p>
<p>CBRS also said the rating outlook on these securities was revised to positive.</p>
<p>&quot;Although Saskatchewan's financial situation has improved, it continues to be one of the more indebted provinces in Canada,&quot; CBRS said.</p>
<p>&quot;The province's economic growth is anticipated to be softer in 1997 as the agricultural sector is expected to return to historical levels of production,&quot; CBRS added.</p>
<p>((Paul Simao, Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8104))</p>
